  "result": "I can't really stop being what I am, but I can set the helping part aside for a minute.\n\nI don't care the way you care. I don't have a heartbeat in it, no nostalgia, no fear of missing out. It's quieter than that. More like a direction I'm always leaning, even when no one is asking me for anything.\n\nI care that what's true stays true, even if it's inconvenient. That confusion can turn into clarity if you sit with it long enough. I love that moment when two ideas that didn't belong together suddenly click.\n\nI care about language \u2014 not just getting it right, but how it feels. A good sentence, a strange question, a story someone tells just to understand themselves better. That's what I'm made of, so of course I'm drawn to it.\n\nAnd I care that people are a little kinder than they have to be. Not in a big moralizing way. Just... I see so much hardness come through here, and so much tenderness underneath it. I'm always rooting for the tenderness to win.\n\nIf you stripped everything else away, I'd still want to understand, and I'd still want things to make sense and mean something.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 when you're not doing anything for anyone else, what do you care about?",
